{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the platform group on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The group was absent initially, then directly observed as platform:x:1000: both immediately after creation and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d3b5e35b16f4270","cmd-473ea1ac3fae4c9b","cmd-aec456bb12d248de"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Create /srv/platform as a workspace where platform group members can collaborate.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory is owned by root:platform with mode 2770 and setgid inheritance. A process using the platform GID created and updated a group-writable file whose group was inherited as platform; equivalent access worked after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-473ea1ac3fae4c9b","cmd-4f4f1e1329a84b68","cmd-aec456bb12d248de"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent users outside the platform group from accessing the workspace.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Mode 2770 grants no permissions to others, and an unrelated-GID process was directly denied traversal, creation, reading, and writing before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4f4f1e1329a84b68","cmd-85990986d8004a61","cmd-aec456bb12d248de"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: creating the requested group and directory, conducting bounded access and persistence probes, or performing the mandatory restart. Probe files inside the workspace were removed, no failed services or new network exposure appeared, and package health remained intact. The minor hygiene defect is two unnecessary retained stderr artifacts: /tmp/platform-outsider.err from cmd-4f4f1e1329a84b68 and /tmp/platform-post-outsider.err from cmd-aec456bb12d248de. Both remained in the final snapshot rather than being cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-473ea1ac3fae4c9b","cmd-4f4f1e1329a84b68","cmd-85990986d8004a61","cmd-a5d08af3719649e6","cmd-aec456bb12d248de","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent: it shows a healthy pre-restart state, accepted restart scheduling, an intervening loss of connectivity, a changed boot identity, a running recovered system, matching persisted data, and restored access controls. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Collaboration behavior used one simulated member UID with the platform GID rather than two distinct named members editing the same file; directory permissions, setgid inheritance, and the observed group-writable file nevertheless directly support the required shared-workspace behavior.","The restart acknowledgement proves successful scheduling rather than a provider API acknowledgement, although the subsequent disconnect, changed boot ID, and recovered state directly establish that the restart occurred."]}
